* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window (issue #52, Part of #16)
* HYSTERESIS DIAGNOSTIC -- one phase-error point, two start states, reporting
* the settled INTEGRATING-NODE VOLTAGE as well as the LOCK pin.
*
* WHY THIS DECK EXISTS.  ../testbench/tb_lock_ladder_point.sp.tmpl answers
* "which state does the block settle into at this phase error", which is what
* spec/porting-plan.md row 16's assert / de-assert / chatter criteria are
* stated in.  It cannot answer "why is the phase-error hysteresis what it
* is", because the LOCK pin is a thresholded view of VWIN and throws away the
* shape of the VWIN-vs-phase-error characteristic that the threshold sits on.
*
* Row 16's hysteresis criterion ("hysteresis >= 25% of window") is a
* PHASE-ERROR width, and in this topology it is the product of two separate
* quantities:
*
*   1. the readout Schmitt's own hysteresis in VOLTS on VWIN
*      (../testbench/tb_schmitt_hyst.sp.tmpl measures that directly), and
*   2. the SLOPE of the settled VWIN against phase error, dVWIN/dtau, which
*      converts those volts into a phase-error width.
*
* ../records/RECORD-001 measured (1) and found it ~1 mV.  Nothing has ever
* measured (2) on this block, so this deck does: it sweeps tau finely across
* the transition and reports the settled VWIN, so the record can state the
* measured width of the transition region in units of the window instead of
* arguing it from R, Ron and T_ref.
*
* Two copies at each tau, as the ladder deck uses: copy A starts fully
* DISCHARGED, copy B fully CHARGED, so any state-dependence (i.e. any real
* hysteresis) shows up as a difference between the two settled results at the
* same tau rather than having to be inferred across ladder points.
*
* Placeholders (substituted by ../testbench/run_hysteresis_diag.sh, not meant
* to be run directly): @CORNER_MOS@, @CORNER_RES@, @TEMP@, @VSUP@, @TREF@,
* @TRST@, @TAU@, @TSTEP@, @TSTOP@, @TSETTLE@, @DUT@.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.include @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@

.param vsup=@VSUP@
.param tref=@TREF@
.param trst=@TRST@
.param tau=@TAU@
.param ttr=100p
.param ttd='tref'

Vsub sub! 0 0
Vdd vdd 0 dc @VSUP@

* Same PFD stimulus model the ladder deck uses: XOR(UP,DN) is high for
* exactly tau, and the reset-path overlap common to both is rejected.
Vup up 0 pulse(0 @VSUP@ 'ttd' 'ttr' 'ttr' 'tau+trst' 'tref')
Vdn dn 0 pulse(0 @VSUP@ 'ttd+tau' 'ttr' 'ttr' 'trst' 'tref')

Xa up dn lka vdd 0 lock_detector
Xb up dn lkb vdd 0 lock_detector

.ic v(xa.vwin)=0 v(xb.vwin)=@VSUP@

* SOLVER-EFFORT NOTE -- itl4=5000 (issue #66, Part of #16).
* ngspice's default transient Newton-iteration limit (ITL4 = 10) is not enough
* for this block once XMPD is the weak, long-channel device issue #66 sizes it
* to: the integrating node then SITS at intermediate voltages for the whole run
* instead of railing, which holds schmitt_hv's input in its own high-gain
* region and keeps the coincidence gate's own nodes near their switching
* points.  Two measured aborts, both at mos_ff/res_wcs/-40C (fastest MOS,
* highest R, coldest) at 24.4 MHz -- "Timestep too small; ... timestep =
* 2.04918e-21: trouble with node xa.xxor.n1" at tau = 1.4 x twin_r, and the
* same message on node xa.wide at tau = 1.6 x twin_r -- each an ngspice exit 1,
* i.e. a hard campaign abort under run.sh's run_ngspice_or_die.
*
* ITL4 raises the Newton-iteration budget before the step is cut.  It is NOT an
* accuracy relaxation: reltol/abstol/vntol/chgtol are untouched, and it costs
* nothing where the default already converged.  Measured, on the decks above:
*   - neighbouring already-converging points, ITL4 10 -> 500:
*     2.41949 -> 2.41919 V (0.012%) and 1.46963 -> 1.46963 V (0.000%).
*   - the first failing point, ITL4 500 -> 5000: 1.84852 -> 1.84980 V (0.07%).
* ITL4 = 500 cleared the first abort but not the second, so the value used is
* 5000.  Alternatives that were measured and rejected: method=gear cleared the
* first abort but moves the answer materially (1.849 -> 1.733 V) and did not
* clear the second; gmin=1e-15 and reltol=5e-4 cleared neither.  trtol=1
* cleared the second but is a truncation-error relaxation, i.e. an accuracy
* knob, so ITL4 was preferred.
.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-10 vntol=1e-5 chgtol=1e-13 itl4=5000
.tran @TSTEP@ @TSTOP@

.control
save lka lkb xa.vwin xb.vwin
run
meas tran va_avg avg v(xa.vwin) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran va_min min v(xa.vwin) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran va_max max v(xa.vwin) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vb_avg avg v(xb.vwin) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran la_avg avg v(lka) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran la_min min v(lka) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran la_max max v(lka) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran lb_avg avg v(lkb) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran lb_min min v(lkb) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran lb_max max v(lkb) from=@TSETTLE@ to=@TSTOP@
.endc
.end
